1
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:02,978
Here's the bag.

2
00:00:02,978 --> 00:00:05,978
Will he be OK, Dad?

3
00:00:05,978 --> 00:00:08,934
I hope so.

4
00:00:08,934 --> 00:00:11,912
That's it.

5
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:14,890
That's the way.

6
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:18,268
That's it. There.

7
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:21,566
Oh, it's going to be all right.

8
00:00:21,566 --> 00:00:22,046
That's it.

9
00:00:22,046 --> 00:00:23,486
Wrap him in the blanket, Dad!

10
00:00:23,486 --> 00:00:25,324
That's it. That's it.

11
00:00:25,324 --> 00:00:26,802
It's all right, Albert.

12
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:28,469
You're going to be OK.

13
00:00:28,469 --> 00:00:31,460
I want my daddy!

14
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:32,758
We'll take you to him.

15
00:00:32,758 --> 00:00:38,714
Easy now. Easy does it. That's it.

16
00:00:38,714 --> 00:00:41,692
Your dad is quite a guy.

17
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:44,669
I know, Grandpa.

18
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:45,702
How is he, Philip?

19
00:00:45,702 --> 00:00:46,218
He's asleep.

20
00:00:46,218 --> 00:00:47,647
He's going to be fine.

21
00:00:47,647 --> 00:00:49,647
How can I thank all of you?

22
00:00:49,647 --> 00:00:50,625
Thank my son Robbie.

23
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:52,625
He pulled him out of the water.

24
00:00:52,625 --> 00:00:53,603
I'm very grateful, Robbie.

25
00:00:53,603 --> 00:00:55,478
Dad saved him, not me.

26
00:00:55,478 --> 00:00:59,979
I'm so thankful to all of you.

27
00:00:59,979 --> 00:01:02,937
So long.

28
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:04,537
He's a lucky boy.

29
00:01:04,537 --> 00:01:07,475
Well, what do you say we get back to our fishing?

30
00:01:07,475 --> 00:01:08,493
That's a great idea.

31
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:11,471
Uh-oh. It's probably the hospital.

32
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:15,306
I have to get to a phone.

33
00:01:15,306 --> 00:01:18,094
It probably means we can't stay.

34
00:01:18,094 --> 00:01:18,760
That's OK.

35
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:27,111
One of my patients has a high fever,

36
00:01:27,111 --> 00:01:32,317
and I have to go to the hospital.

37
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:33,317
I'm sorry, Robbie.

38
00:01:33,317 --> 00:01:36,015
I guess I ruined your day.

39
00:01:36,015 --> 00:01:42,851
You didn't ruin my day, Dad.

40
00:01:42,851 --> 00:02:09,220
I understand. I really do.

41
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:12,274
Why are you back so early?

42
00:02:12,274 --> 00:02:14,008
Philip had to go back to the hospital.

43
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:16,797
He had an emergency.

44
00:02:16,797 --> 00:02:17,557
Oh, that's too bad, Robbie.

45
00:02:17,557 --> 00:02:18,986
Did it spoil your fun?

46
00:02:18,986 --> 00:02:22,284
No, Mom. We had a great time.

47
00:02:22,284 --> 00:02:23,369
Well, did you do any fishing?

48
00:02:23,369 --> 00:02:29,315
Yeah, we caught lots of them. Look!

49
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:35,187
They had a special on frozen fish down at the supermarket.

50
00:02:35,187 --> 00:02:37,254
Oh, you really had a bad day.

51
00:02:37,254 --> 00:02:38,499
We had a good day.

52
00:02:38,499 --> 00:02:41,210
Robbie pulled a boy out of the water.

53
00:02:41,210 --> 00:02:44,188
And Dad saved his life.

54
00:02:44,188 --> 00:02:47,766
He's a terrific doctor, Mom.

55
00:02:47,766 --> 00:02:59,345
I know.

56
00:02:59,345 --> 00:03:02,656
Hi, Pop. Hi, Son.

57
00:03:02,656 --> 00:03:04,634
Hello, Dad.

58
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:06,354
What a day!

59
00:03:06,354 --> 00:03:07,404
How about a cup of coffee, Son?

60
00:03:07,404 --> 00:03:10,112
I'd love a cup of coffee.

61
00:03:10,112 --> 00:03:18,045
How was the patient?

62
00:03:18,045 --> 00:03:19,212
She'll be fine.

63
00:03:19,212 --> 00:03:21,176
Was it serious?

64
00:03:21,176 --> 00:03:22,501
No.

65
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:28,457
Until today, I was never really interested in medicine.

66
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:31,435
Well, it's hard work.

67
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:34,413
Now I know.

68
00:03:34,413 --> 00:03:39,171
I had a good time today, Robbie.

69
00:03:39,171 --> 00:03:40,849
Me, too.

70
00:03:40,849 --> 00:03:44,487
Why don't we do it again?

71
00:03:44,487 --> 00:03:46,047
Can we? When?

72
00:03:46,047 --> 00:03:47,325
How about next Saturday?

73
00:03:47,325 --> 00:03:50,803
Won't you be busy?

74
00:03:50,803 --> 00:03:53,201
I'm changing my schedule.

75
00:03:53,201 --> 00:03:56,339
Well, do we have a date?

76
00:03:56,339 --> 00:03:58,570
We sure do, Dad.

77
00:03:58,570 --> 00:04:00,237
Grandpa, can you come?

78
00:04:00,237 --> 00:04:03,655
I have other plans, Robbie.

79
00:04:03,655 --> 00:04:07,571
But I think you two can have a good time together without me.

80
00:04:07,571 --> 00:04:10,571
No, Dad, and certainly not without the right magic.
